{"title":"Career Roadmap · School Teacher (TGT/PGT)","role":"School Teacher (TGT/PGT)","summary":"A School Teacher is responsible for designing and delivering classroom instruction, assessing student learning, supporting individual development and contributing to the academic and overall development of students.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Ed (Bachelor of Education)","Course":"B.Ed - Subject Pedagogy (Science / Maths / Social Studies / Languages / Commerce)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A School Teacher is responsible for designing and delivering classroom instruction, assessing student learning, supporting individual development and contributing to the academic and overall development of students."},{"type":"p","text":"The TGT (Trained Graduate Teacher) and PGT (Post Graduate Teacher) pathways generally differ by educational qualification, subject level and recruitment rules."},{"type":"h","text":"TGT"},{"type":"p","text":"Typically teaches middle/secondary school classes, with eligibility depending on the recruiting authority and subject."},{"type":"h","text":"PGT"},{"type":"p","text":"Generally teaches senior-secondary classes and usually requires a relevant postgraduate subject qualification plus teacher-education qualification, subject to the applicable recruitment rules."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lesson planning"},{"text":"Classroom teaching"},{"text":"Student assessment"},{"text":"Activity-based learning"},{"text":"Assignments and projects"},{"text":"Remedial teaching"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Student mentoring"},{"text":"Digital learning"},{"text":"Academic documentation"},{"text":"Co-curricular activities"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"B.Ed is a teacher-education qualification, but TGT/PGT eligibility is not determined by B.Ed alone. Recruitment authorities 