erative AI"},{"type":"p","text":"Teachers can use AI to accelerate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lesson Design"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Activity Creation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Assessment Creation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Differentiation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Feedback Drafting"},{"text":"But teachers must verify accuracy, originality, age suitability, privacy and curriculum alignment."}]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile at Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong teacher candidate should ideally demonstrate:"},{"type":"h","text":"Subject"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong subject knowledge"},{"text":"Conceptual clarity"},{"text":"Problem-solving"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Pedagogy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lesson planning"},{"text":"Teaching methodology"},{"text":"Active learning"},{"text":"Differentiated instruction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Classroom"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Classroom management"},{"text":"Student engagement"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Mentoring"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Assessment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Question-paper design"},{"text":"Rubrics"},{"text":"Formative assessment"},{"text":"Remedial teaching"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"LMS"},{"text":"Digital resources"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"AI-assisted teaching"},{"text":"Online assessment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Child safeguarding awareness"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Teamwork"},{"text":"Continuous professional development"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong Subject Knowledge"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"B.Ed Pedagogy"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Lesson Planning"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Classroom Management"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Student Assessment"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Remedial Teaching"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Inclusive Education"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Communication & Presentation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Digital Teaching"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"AI Literacy"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Learning Analytics"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Student Mentoring"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Parent / Stakeholder Communication"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Action Research"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Relevant Bachelor's Degree","B.Ed","Teaching Practicum","Required Eligibility/Recruitment Requirements","TGT/School Teacher","Subject Expertise + Digital Teaching","Senior Teacher","PGT/Academic Coordinator","HOD","Vice Principal/Principal"]},{"type":"p","text":"For maximum employability, the student should combine strong subject knowledge + B.Ed pedagogy + classroom management + assessment expertise + digital teaching + AI literacy + inclusive education + communication + continuous professional development."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-fitment mapping note","text":"The database should distinguish TGT and PGT eligibility rather than treating them as identical outcomes. TGT recruitment generally depends on the relevant graduation subject and applicable teacher-eligibility/recruitment requirements, while PGT positions commonly require a relevant postgraduate subject qualification in addition to teacher-education requirements. Exact eligibility varies by school board, state, central recruiting authority and subject."}]}]}